# family: display
# bridge: A(value-parity)
# regime: continuous readings agree to 6 digits, tick-domain values exact
# instrument-first: c4f11bda
# baseline: tests/unit/interpolation
# baseline-count: 34
#
# The unit is the display data plane: the projection helper, the per value
# interpolation spec, and the channel history that resamples one value stream.
# The file mixed two planes and this batch carved one out, exactly as liveness
# and scenes did before it.
#
# WHAT DID NOT CROSS HAS SHRUNK SINCE, and a reason below that still names
# DisplayCore whole is stale on its face. The book, the runtime row, the
# channel row, the writer port, the render offset, the per-channel pass
# verdict, the pump transition verdict and the role LADDER
# (NetwDisplayRoleFacts) are all native. What is left in display_core.gd is
# the pump LOOP, the channel-table build that reads Nodes and sync channels,
# the role facts it gathers from them, and the CHASE pump's read of the live
# predicted body, which the plan of record fixes as permanent Ring 2.
#
# THE DEPENDENCY DECIDED THE ORDER. NetwDisplayHistory names NetwInterpolate for
# its mode and NetwProject for its tail, so both crossed first, in their own
# slice, under the migration recipe's readiness rule. Neither had a unit suite
# of its own except NetwProject's four cases, so the spec class arrives with
# native laws it never had in GDScript rather than with none.
#
# CLASSDB FLATTENED THE ENUMS, which is the one forced API change.
# `NetwInterpolate.Mode.LERP` has no spelling for a registered class, so every
# call site reads `NetwInterpolate.MODE_LERP` and a `mode: NetwInterpolate.Mode`
# parameter reads `int`. Fourteen sites. The history's last-sample flags moved
# the same way, from members to bound getters, because `is_sleeping` cannot be
# both a member and a getter: `history.is_sleeping` -> `history.sleeping`,
# `last_projected` -> `has_projected()`, `last_project_age` ->
# `get_project_age()`, `snapped` -> `has_snapped()`, `.buffer` ->
# `get_buffer()`.
#
# THE PORT FOUND A LIVE DEFECT, which is the reason `get_at` exists on the
# native class at all. `_pump_history` read a sibling channel's derivative with
# `sibling.history.get_at(...)` and `_History` had no such method, so every
# `project_by` channel under a FORECAST timeline called a method that was never
# there. Nothing caught it because the branch needs forecast on, a non-empty
# sibling, and a playhead past the newest tick all at once. GDScript let it
# ship; the compiler would not.
#
# THE ARM AND ITS GOLDEN SURVIVE, unlike the interest batch's. The claim here is
# float parity over a resampling function rather than a set of properties over
# integers, so the 47-row trace recorded at c4f11bda is evidence a property
# cannot restate. It was red-proven on eight independent halves: the gap
# threshold and its strictness, the forecast age clamp, record deduplication,
# the angle mode, the snap escape, the sleep latch, the explicit derivative, and
# the smoothing weight. Two probes did not move a row and both were read rather
# than ignored. The first was a real hole, a gap scenario that only ever took
# the wide branch and so passed against any threshold below its gap, and it grew
# the two straddling gaps that close it. The second is not a hole and no rows can
# close it: Godot dispatches `lerp` on a Quaternion to the same spherical walk
# `slerp` runs, so the two rotation modes are indistinguishable by observation.
#
# The golden's numbers are ALSO inlined into display_history_tests.cpp, so the
# tier reads them every run rather than leaving them in a file nothing opens.
# The arm stays runnable as the whole-trace check the per-case restatement
# cannot be.
#
# THE PURITY LINT CARRIES WITH ITS CLASS REGIONS REMOVED. It reads
# display_core.gd as a string and asserts forbidden tokens are absent from the
# pure kernels. `class _History:` and `class _Playhead:` are both gone, and the
# lint would have failed loudly rather than passing vacuously, which is the
# right way round. Their successor is structural: display_history.cpp and
# display_playhead.cpp include no engine header that could reach a tree, a
# clock or a signal, and tools/check_sources.py holds every source to
# compiling. `func _calculate_min_lag(` left the kernel list with the same
# argument, as `NetwDisplayPlayhead.min_lag`.
#
